From e27f38547452a97a81475c862aafa7069368a7b7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 14 Jul 2026 08:23:55 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] MOS recall fixes: voxel label aggregation, threshold
 selection, Tversky, point-level eval

Address the recall-limited operating point (val P~0.92 / R~0.64 -> IoU ~0.62):

- semantickitti.py: collapse duplicate voxels by max motion priority
  (moving > static > ignore) instead of keeping the first point, so a voxel
  is moving whenever any of its points is. Add opt-in return_point_map with
  full-resolution reference labels + point->voxel index for point-level eval.
- collate.py: forward the point map, offsetting voxel indices per sample.
- metrics.py: MovingThresholdMeter sweeps softmax cutoffs and reports the
  IoU-optimal threshold (the model has large precision headroom below 0.5).
- train.py: validate() selects best.pt by threshold-optimal moving IoU and
  saves the chosen threshold in the checkpoint; logs argmax IoU alongside.
- model.py: stop detaching the offset head so its aux loss can shape the
  shared backbone.
- eval_mos_official.py: --point-level propagates each voxel prediction to all
  reference points (official protocol) and --threshold applies the tuned cutoff.
- configs/residual_v3.yaml: Tversky on (a=0.3, b=0.7) and semantic_weight 0.3.
- .gitignore: ignore Python bytecode caches.
